    "version": 1,
    "task": "Make `git gloss ary` one document: the review desk served by ary, with the branch, base and revision pickers in the desk's own top bar (no iframe shell, no second sidebar)",
    "summary": "`/` now renders the desk page for /?rev=&head=&base= (302 to the canonical URL when no rev); the refs travel in the page JSON as an optional `ary` block, and src/ary/picker.js is spliced into the nonce'd script only in that mode, so `html` pages change only by the sticky top bar and rail sizing fix (shared CSS, plus a ResizeObserver) and are otherwise unchanged, and the CSP is unchanged. The old shell, /view, /api/refs, /api/log and /ary.js|css are removed. Dropped on purpose: the commit list with search and Load more, the per-commit gloss/reviewed marks list, the Reload/open-in-tab bar. Also dropped: the wip row's stale warning and glossed mark (wipStaleness/notedCommits are no longer called). Also dropped: the pickers' wip choice; wip opens only when / is opened with nothing chosen, or by typing `wip` in the revision box.",
    "groups": [
      {
        "id": "desk-route",
        "intent": "Serve the desk at / from ?rev=&head=&base=, redirecting to the canonical URL",
        "necessity": "required",
        "serves": "task",
        "removal_impact": "ary would have no page to serve without the old shell",
        "evidence": "test/ary.test.ts 'ary serves the desk page itself ...'",
        "impact": "contract",
        "impact_reason": "the URL scheme and request handling of the server change; / replaces /view, /api/*",
        "hunks": [
          "h10:1-5,9-65",
          "h11:1-4,19-21",
          "h12:1-2"
        ],
        "notes": "Ports the old client load() rules to the server: wip first only when nothing at all is chosen, else base..head if it has commits, else the head's newest commit as a sha; a deleted head or base renders with a notice instead of redirecting. head/base are only trusted if they name a known branch; they only pick pickers' values and the default rev. Page CSP is the same nonce policy as `html` (no connect-src: no fetch); the HTTP header adds frame-ancestors 'none'. Host check, GET/HEAD only, revParam validation, MAX_RANGE_COMMITS and no-store are untouched. A branch more than MAX_RANGE_COMMITS ahead of its base falls back to its newest commit instead of an error page; an explicit oversized ?rev= still gets the 422."
